---
name: gates-report-truth
description: The difference between a failing gate and a gate that could not run in {{PROJECT_NAME}}
metadata:
  type: project
---

Every gate script emits exactly one JSON line. Two shapes matter and they mean
opposite things:

- `{"pass":false, ...}` — the gate ran and the game did not satisfy it.
- `{"pass":false,"error_kind":"godot_not_found", ...}` — the gate could not run.
  Other kinds: `python_missing`, `harness_missing`, `not_style_locked`,
  `profile_unknown`.

**Why it matters:** treating the second as the first sends an agent off to fix a
game that is not broken. Treating it as a pass ships something nobody checked.
Both mistakes destroy the reason gates exist.

**How to apply:** an `error_kind` stops the affected part of the run and is
reported as an environment problem. Never approximate a gate that could not run,
never claim a pass without the JSON line that shows it, and quote the line
verbatim rather than paraphrasing it — the line names the specific rule, and the
paraphrase loses it. See [[sim-render-split]] for the determinism gate this
protects.
